1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,376
一只椋鸟，看不见整个鸟群
A single starling can't see the flock.

2
00:00:03,376 --> 00:00:05,852
它只盯着身边的六七只同伴
It only watches the six or seven birds beside it.

3
00:00:06,412 --> 00:00:08,590
可几十万只这样的鸟聚在一起
Yet put a few hundred thousand of them together,

4
00:00:08,590 --> 00:00:10,632
就能在天上画出这样的形状
and they paint shapes like this across the sky.

5
00:00:12,292 --> 00:00:14,642
没有领头鸟，也没有指挥
No leader, no conductor.

6
00:00:14,642 --> 00:00:17,665
1986 年，有人只用三条规则
In 1986, someone used just three rules

7
00:00:17,665 --> 00:00:20,015
就在电脑里复现了这一幕
to recreate it on a computer.

8
00:00:20,775 --> 00:00:25,036
这一期，我们从一只鸟出发，一路演进到六万只
This episode, we start from one bird and evolve all the way to sixty thousand.

9
00:00:26,536 --> 00:00:28,229
他叫克雷格·雷诺兹
His name is Craig Reynolds.

10
00:00:28,229 --> 00:00:31,757
他把模拟出来的鸟叫作 Boids，“类鸟体”
He called his simulated birds boids: bird-oid objects.

11
00:00:32,017 --> 00:00:34,942
每只 boid 只感知身边一小圈邻居
Each boid senses only the neighbors in a small radius,

12
00:00:34,942 --> 00:00:36,056
只做三件事
and does just three things:

13
00:00:36,416 --> 00:00:38,819
分离，离得太近就躲开
separation: steer away when someone gets too close;

14
00:00:39,479 --> 00:00:42,173
对齐，方向跟邻居保持一致
alignment: match your neighbors' heading;

15
00:00:42,833 --> 00:00:45,242
聚合，朝邻居的中心靠拢
cohesion: move toward their center.

16
00:00:46,002 --> 00:00:49,163
三股力相加，就是这一帧的转向
Add the three forces, and that's this frame's steering.

17
00:00:49,163 --> 00:00:52,324
没有全局规划，鸟群自己出现了
No global plan, yet the flock simply emerges.

18
00:00:52,784 --> 00:00:55,931
1992 年，它登上了《蝙蝠侠归来》
In 1992 it reached Batman Returns,

19
00:00:55,931 --> 00:00:58,329
生成了成群的蝙蝠和企鹅大军
driving swarms of bats and an army of penguins.

20
00:00:59,429 --> 00:01:02,364
1999 年的 GDC 上
At GDC 1999,

21
00:01:02,364 --> 00:01:05,666
雷诺兹把它扩展成一整套转向行为
Reynolds expanded it into a whole toolkit of steering behaviors:

22
00:01:05,666 --> 00:01:08,234
寻找、逃离、徘徊、避障
seek, flee, wander, avoid.

23
00:01:08,494 --> 00:01:12,721
核心只有一行：期望速度，减去当前速度
The core is a single line: desired velocity minus current velocity.

24
00:01:13,181 --> 00:01:16,440
放进一只鹰，每只鸟多一条“逃离”
Drop in a hawk and give each bird one extra flee rule,

25
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:19,185
鸟群就会被撕开，再重新合拢
and the flock tears open, then closes again.

26
00:01:19,945 --> 00:01:21,711
《半条命》里的异星飞鸟
In Half-Life, the alien flyers of Xen

27
00:01:21,711 --> 00:01:23,476
名字就直接叫 Boid
are literally named Boid.

28
00:01:24,876 --> 00:01:27,386
但这里藏着一个规模问题
But a scaling problem hides here:

29
00:01:27,386 --> 00:01:30,614
每只鸟都得先找出，谁是它的邻居
every bird first has to find out who its neighbors are.

30
00:01:30,874 --> 00:01:33,122
和所有鸟逐一比距离
Compare against every other bird,

31
00:01:33,122 --> 00:01:36,118
一千只鸟，每帧就是一百万次
and a thousand birds cost a million checks per frame;

32
00:01:36,118 --> 00:01:38,928
数量翻十倍，开销翻一百倍
ten times the birds, a hundred times the cost.

33
00:01:39,388 --> 00:01:44,079
解法是空间网格：每只鸟只查自己和相邻的格子
The fix is a spatial grid: each bird checks only its own cell and the cells next to it,

34
00:01:44,079 --> 00:01:47,793
开销从 n 的平方，降到接近 n
and the cost drops from n squared to roughly n.

35
00:01:48,253 --> 00:01:52,144
2006 年，雷诺兹靠它在 PS3 上
In 2006, Reynolds used it to run

36
00:01:52,144 --> 00:01:55,505
跑起了一万五千个个体，每秒六十帧
fifteen thousand agents on a PS3 at sixty frames per second.

37
00:01:56,605 --> 00:01:58,634
那真实的椋鸟看多远？
So how far does a real starling look?

38
00:01:58,634 --> 00:02:02,015
2008 年，STARFLAG 团队
In 2008, the STARFLAG team

39
00:02:02,015 --> 00:02:04,889
重建了鸟群里每只鸟的三维位置
rebuilt the 3D position of every bird in a flock.

40
00:02:05,149 --> 00:02:07,157
答案是：不按距离
The answer: not by distance.

41
00:02:07,157 --> 00:02:10,807
只看最近的六七只，不管它们离得多远
Each bird tracks its six or seven nearest, however far away.

42
00:02:11,267 --> 00:02:12,779
这叫拓扑邻居
These are topological neighbors.

43
00:02:12,779 --> 00:02:15,466
论文的模拟显示：密度剧变时
The paper's simulations show that when density swings,

44
00:02:15,466 --> 00:02:17,649
这样的鸟群更不容易散
such flocks are harder to break apart.

45
00:02:18,949 --> 00:02:21,423
再往上，就得交给 GPU
Beyond that, hand it to the GPU:

46
00:02:21,423 --> 00:02:25,545
每只鸟的位置和速度，存成浮点纹理里的一个像素
each bird's position and velocity is one pixel of a float texture.

47
00:02:25,905 --> 00:02:28,068
邻居也不再一个个去数
Neighbors are no longer counted one by one;

48
00:02:28,068 --> 00:02:30,564
先把所有鸟累加进一张网格
every bird is splatted into a grid

49
00:02:30,564 --> 00:02:33,559
记下每格的数量、中心和平均速度
that keeps each cell's count, center and average velocity.

50
00:02:33,919 --> 00:02:36,081
每只鸟只读周围的格子
Each bird reads only the cells around it,

51
00:02:36,081 --> 00:02:39,240
三条规则，就变成了对一张场的采样
and the three rules become samples of a field.

52
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:41,865
六万五千五百三十六只
Sixty-five thousand five hundred thirty-six birds,

53
00:02:41,865 --> 00:02:44,586
每一只都在实时做着同样的三件事
each doing the same three things, in real time.

54
00:02:47,286 --> 00:02:50,985
从三条规则到六万只，规则几乎没变
From three rules to sixty thousand birds, the rules barely changed.

55
00:02:50,985 --> 00:02:53,711
变的是我们怎么组织数据
What changed is how we organize the data.

56
00:02:53,971 --> 00:02:56,526
可如果每一只不再是一个点
But what if each one isn't a point anymore,

57
00:02:56,526 --> 00:02:59,421
而是一条有骨骼、会摆尾的鱼呢？
but a fish with a skeleton and a swinging tail?

58
00:02:59,821 --> 00:03:02,021
每条鱼大概有 60 到 100 个关节
there's like 60 to 100 joints

59
00:03:02,021 --> 00:03:04,571
每一帧，你都得把每条鱼的关节全部更新一遍
and every frame you have to update all of those joints per fish

60
00:03:04,571 --> 00:03:07,571
所以要更新的不只是一万条鱼
so instead of just having 10,000 fish to update

61
00:03:07,571 --> 00:03:10,621
而是一万乘以一百个关节，这太疯狂了
you have ten thousand times 100 joints, which is crazy

62
00:03:11,121 --> 00:03:14,151
下一期，我们潜进《ABZÛ》的海底
Next time, we dive into the sea of ABZÛ

63
00:03:14,151 --> 00:03:16,423
看上万条鱼怎么游出生命感
to see how ten thousand fish come alive.

64
00:03:16,683 --> 00:03:19,163
而这一切，还得从一只鸟说起
And all of it starts, once again, with a single bird.
